{"name":"Carmelito","hex":"#bb534c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Carmelito, California","blocks":[{"text":"Carmelito was a planned settlement, initially called Point Lobos City, on Point Lobos in Monterey County, California, United States. It was located just north of Carmel Highlands and about 3 miles (4.8 km) south of Carmel on Highway 1. Sited on the former Rancho San Jose y Sur Chiquito, the Carmelo Land and Coal Company planned the subdivision in 1890 when their coal mine on nearby Malpaso Creek proved to be unprofitable. It subdivided the land into 1,000 parcels, which began selling lots for $25 to $50. The lack of a bridge across the Carmel River and two national economic recessions during the 1890s combined to severely restrict sales. Only a few small cabins were built."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmelito%2C_California","wikidata":"Q5043364"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Two blue water meters on a matte red painted brick facade with pipes in Seoul","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Two_blue_water_meters_on_a_matte_red_painted_brick_facade_with_pipes_in_Seoul.jpg/500px-Two_blue_water_meters_on_a_matte_red_painted_brick_facade_with_pipes_in_Seoul.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Two_blue_water_meters_on_a_matte_red_painted_brick_facade_with_pipes_in_Seoul.jpg","share":0.244375},{"title":"Woman's shirt from Kutch, Gujarat, India, IMA 55114","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Woman%27s_shirt_from_Kutch%2C_Gujarat%2C_India%2C_IMA_55114.jpg/500px-Woman%27s_shirt_from_Kutch%2C_Gujarat%2C_India%2C_IMA_55114.jpg","ratio":0.9394273127753304,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Woman%27s_shirt_from_Kutch,_Gujarat,_India,_IMA_55114.jpg","share":0.126875},{"title":"Exterior spherical lantern on a matte red painted brick facade in Seoul","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th